  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="note"><strong>Choice and privacy:</strong> you do not need to share real names, ages, family structure, living arrangements, photos, or coworker information. Use the fictional people on this page, public fictional characters, or an invented family whenever you prefer.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A close family:</b> Name four real, pictured, or invented people with a full sentence each. <span class="ex">This is Carla, a parent. This is her son, Luis.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A fictional household:</b> Choose who lives in one invented home. <span class="ex">Maya lives with her partner and their two children.</span> &nbsp;<span class="ex">Leo lives with his grandparent.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>An invented coworker's family:</b> Use a name, a possessive adjective, and possessive <span class="ex">'s</span>. <span class="ex">Omar has a spouse, Leyla. Omar's cousin lives nearby. Their child is six.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>A fictional family picture:</b> Point and name each labeled person. <span class="ex">This is the grandmother. These are her two children.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Ask and answer in role:</b> Choose a fictional identity. Answer in full sentences: <span class="ex">Do you have siblings? How many cousins do you have? Who is the oldest person in this family?</span></div>

